<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>For You 💖</title>

<style>
body{
  margin:0;
  padding:0;
  font-family: 'Segoe UI', sans-serif;
  text-align:center;
  background: linear-gradient(135deg,#ffd6e8,#e0f7fa);
}

.container{
  padding:30px 15px;
}

img.hero{
  width:220px;
  border-radius:20px;
  box-shadow:0 12px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.2);
  margin-bottom:20px;
}

h2{
  color:#ff4d6d;
  margin-bottom:20px;
}

button{
  padding:12px 26px;
  border:none;
  border-radius:30px;
  background:#ff4d6d;
  color:white;
  font-size:16px;
  cursor:pointer;
  box-shadow:0 6px 15px rgba(255,77,109,0.4);
}

.card{
  background:white;
  padding:25px;
  border-radius:20px;
  margin:25px auto;
  max-width:420px;
  display:none;
  box-shadow:0 15px 35px rgba(255,77,109,0.25);
  animation:fade 0.6s ease;
}

@keyframes fade{
  from{opacity:0; transform:translateY(20px);}
  to{opacity:1; transform:translateY(0);}
}
</style>
</head>

<body>

<div class="container">

  <!-- Cute couple image -->
  <img class="hero" src="https://i.pinimg.com/564x/3b/78/42/3b7842c80c0b7c7a2c4b7fbdba9e3c65.jpg">

  <h2>Just for you 💝</h2>

  <button onclick="next()">Tap slowly 😉</button>

  <div class="card">
    I can love you for 4 days<br>
    Spring, Summer, Autumn, Winter<br><br>

    Oh no…<br>
    Maybe 3 days<br>
    Yesterday, Today, Tomorrow<br><br>

    How about 2 days<br>
    Day and Night<br><br>

    Maybe one day is enough<br>
    Everyday
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    If one day you ask me how much I love you<br><br>

    I love three things in the world<br>
    The sun, the moon, and you<br><br>

    The sun for the morning<br>
    The moon for the night<br>
    And you… forever 💖
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    Why I like you?<br><br>
    You have a calm, genuine vibe<br>
    And honestly… your smile is a little addictive 😌
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    Maybe someday…<br>
    Random talks, shared laughs,<br>
    and keeping things simple & real 🌸
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    Secret 🤫<br><br>
    If you’re still reading this,<br>
    I guess you smiled.<br><br>
    And if you smiled,<br>
    maybe I’m doing something right 😉
  </div>

</div>

<script>
let i = 0;
function next(){
  let cards = document.getElementsByClassName("card");
  if(i < cards.length){
    cards[i].style.display = "block";
    i++;
  }
}
</script>

</body>
</html>
